# `turns += 1` and, in an arm, `last = i` stand in front of `into[i] = ..`. The store into the list needs a test, and where the test fails the turn begins again in the closed copy; a turn that had stored into a variable of its file could not, so the list was stored into as written, and read as written with it.
# The variables of files that the text of the loop stores are read at the head of each turn of the typed copy. A store into one of them leaves the turn able to begin again, also where the ways of a branch meet; where it begins again each is stored back, so that the closed copy counts the turn once.
# f1 = running
